    "updated": "2026-10-04",
    "answer": "Apple HealthKit stores mood and emotion logs as HKStateOfMind samples, available from iOS 18.0, watchOS 11.0, macOS 15.0 and visionOS 2.0, and Apple's June 2024 update note says apps can read and write them. Each sample carries a kind (dailyMood or momentaryEmotion), a numeric valence, a seven-step valenceClassification, a list of labels such as anxious or calm, and a list of associations such as work or family. Apple's reference pages for these symbols give declarations only, with no stated valence range or label definitions. Google's Health Connect data types page lists no mood or emotion record; its only Wellness record is MindfulnessSessionRecord, which logs a session, not a feeling.",
