    "answer": "Apple HealthKit exposes health records that people download from supported healthcare institutions as read-only HKClinicalRecord samples, each wrapping one FHIR resource as an HKFHIRResource whose JSON you parse yourself. Apple documents nine clinical type identifiers, from allergyRecord to coverageRecord, and two FHIR releases, DSTU2 and R4. Access needs the Clinical Health Records capability (the health-records value of the com.apple.developer.healthkit.access entitlement) and the NSHealthClinicalHealthRecordsShareUsageDescription key, and Apple warns that App Review may reject apps that enable the capability without using the data. SMART Health Cards and EU Digital COVID Certificates arrive separately as HKVerifiableClinicalRecord, through a query that needs its own entitlement.",
